--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -43 +43 @@ Two axes matter:
-`background` means headless. Pi starts a `pi -p` child process without opening a pane.
+`background` means headless. For a named Pi agent, Pi starts a `pi -p` child process without opening a pane.
@@ -1002,0 +1003,30 @@ Zellij 0.44.x needs a short focus transaction for directional and stacked placem
+## Background runner API for companion extensions
+
+A trusted Pi extension can submit a report-only background job. This is an in-process `pi.events` API, not a Pi tool, child-session format, or process launcher. Like `/subagents`, the API is available only when at least one named agent is enabled. A submitted job does not use that agent.
+
+From an extension command, emit `pi-subagents:background-runner:v1:submit` with this payload and check for a synchronous reply before the handler continues:
+
+```ts
+type Report = {
+  ok: boolean;
+  report: string;
+  saveReport?: boolean;
+  cleanupWarning?: string;
+};
+
+type Reply = { id: string; completion: Promise<void> } | { error: string };
+
+type Submission = {
+  name: string;
+  title: string;
+  timeoutSeconds: number;
+  run: (input: { cwd: string; signal: AbortSignal }) => Promise<Report>;
+  reply: (result: Reply) => void;
+};
+```
+
+- `name` is a lower-kebab handle of at most 32 characters; `title` is a printable label of at most 100 characters. `timeoutSeconds` is a whole-run wall-clock budget (0.001 to 2147483.647 seconds).
+- An absent reply means that v1 is unavailable; show an error rather than falling back to another execution path. An `{ error }` reply means the request was rejected without starting the job. An accepted reply provides the run ID and a completion promise; clients without UI can await it. Neither package needs to be loaded first.
+- The fork supplies the origin session's `cwd` and `AbortSignal` and tracks the job in `/subagents` under the shared concurrency limit. It aborts on timeout, kill, or origin-session shutdown. The callback must observe abort, release its external resources (including subprocesses), and settle **after** cleanup; Pi cannot forcibly interrupt arbitrary extension code. The slot remains occupied while cleanup runs. Aborted runs cannot report success; an optional `cleanupWarning` is retained even if the normal report was discarded.
+- Return a nonempty, render-safe `report` and mark partial/failed reports with `ok: false`. If `saveReport` is set and the parent has a session path, the report is also saved as `<name>-<id>.md` in the normal session artifact directory. No report is saved or delivered after the origin starts closing. Otherwise the report is displayed in the origin session without triggering a model turn. There is no child transcript, model accounting, or resume action.
+
